  <data name="GameMode_X01_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>X01</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_X01_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Score down from the start score to exactly zero. Going below zero (or leaving 1 with a double/master out) is a bust and the visit does not count.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Cricket_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cricket</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Cricket_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hit 15–20 and the bull three times each to open them. Extra hits on an open number score points while an opponent still has it open. Close everything with the most points to win.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_CutThroatCricket_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cut Throat Cricket</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_CutThroatCricket_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Like Cricket, but points on your open numbers are given to every opponent who hasn't closed them. Close everything with the fewest points to win.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_NoScoreCricket_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No Score Cricket</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_NoScoreCricket_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pure race: the first player to close 15–20 and the bull wins. No points are scored.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_AroundTheClock_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Around the Clock</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_AroundTheClock_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hit 1, 2, 3 … up to 20 in order. Any segment of the current number counts. First to hit 20 wins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Shanghai_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Shanghai</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Shanghai_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Round N targets number N. Singles, doubles and triples of the target score their value. Hitting single, double and triple of the target in one visit is a Shanghai and wins immediately.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_CountUp_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Count Up</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_CountUp_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Every dart adds its value. First player to reach the target score wins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_HighScore_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>High Score</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_HighScore_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Every dart adds its value. Highest total after the last round wins.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_HalveIt_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Halve It</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_HalveIt_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Each round has a target (15, 16, any double, 17, 18, any triple, 19, 20, bull). Hits on the target score points; miss it with all three darts and your score is halved.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Bob27_Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bob's 27</value>
    <comment>Established game name; usually kept in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="GameMode_Bob27_Rules" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Start with 27. Round N targets double N (then the bull). Each hit adds the double's value; missing all three darts subtracts it. Drop to zero or below and you're out.</value>
  </data>
